<title>RUSSIA: UES scraps one pct voting share limit.</title>
<headline>UES scraps one pct voting share limit.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders at Russia's biggest company, national power group UES, abolished at Friday's annual meeting a company rule limiting single investors to one percent of the voting shares.</p>
<p>Previously shareholders needed written permission from the company to acquire and exercise more than one percent of the voting shares.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
